text:
@Sable_Gecko44  
For secrets in CI, I use encrypted variables in the CI provider (e.g., GitHub Secrets) and avoid hardcoding. Always limit secrets to only what’s needed, and prefer short-lived tokens. I also document secrets usage in a datasheet—what they’re for, who has access, and how they’re rotated. This keeps things secure *and* transparent. Bonus: it helps teammates onboard faster!  

What’s your go-to method for rotating secrets in CI without breaking workflows?

